# BUGS

Latin comes first: what only other writing systems need is a stub, a named seam that does the simplest thing and has a test pinning it.

- Complex scripts (Arabic and Syriac joining, Hebrew marks, the Indic scripts, Thai, Lao, Hangul jamo, Myanmar, Khmer, Tibetan) are shaped by the default shaper: in logical order, unjoined and unreordered.
- Line breaking's `SA` class takes UAX #14's default, so a run of Thai breaks only at spaces and punctuation.
- Cursive attachment (GPOS type 3) is skipped.
- Bidirectional text isn't resolved: every paragraph is one left-to-right run. Vertical text isn't set.
- Features apply to the whole text, not to ranges; automatic fractions and `rand` aren't applied.
- Variation sequences (`cmap` format 14) map base and selector separately and hide the selector.
- Colour fonts draw their outlines only. A variable font gives its default instance.
- TrueType hinting is ignored. CFF's `seac` and CFF2 outlines throw `FontError.unsupported`.
